Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:08:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] sovereignos: keep the keyboard inside the cutout and
 system-bar insets in landscape

The platform lays the input method window out inside the display cutout, so in landscape an empty strip beside the keyboard shows the app instead of the keyboard background. The window is now laid out under the cutout, where the platform pads its content root by the cutout and system-bar insets, so the keys stay where they were. The keyboard background moves from the input view, which is as tall as the screen, to the window background and is drawn from the top of the keyboard down over the whole width. The insets and the touchable region are computed in window coordinates, and the key preview, the popup panels and the gesture trail are placed relative to the content view that holds them. The measurement is recorded in docs/research/keyboard-landscape-inset-investigation.md. ADR-146.
